Having this list of parameters effectively duplicated seems error-prone when we will (inevitably) add more parameters.

Could we perhaps rewrite the `ReadCSV` function below to iterate over the `kwargs`, e.g. something like:

```cpp
for(auto &arg : kwargs) {
   auto &arg_name = arg.first;
   if (arg_name == "header") {
        ...
   } else if (arg_name == "compression") {
        ...
   } else {
        throw Exception("Unrecognized parameter X");
   }
}
```
